\begin{align*}
x_1 + x_2 + x_3 &= 3a - 6,\\
x_1x_2 + x_2x_3 + x_3x_1 &= 21,\\
x_1x_2x_3 &= -(a).
\end{align*}
Since $x_1$, $x_2$, $x_3$ are the roots of the polynomial and they are an arithmetic sequence, we have $x_1 + x_3 = 2x_2$, so $x_2 = 2$. Thus,
\begin{align*}
3a - 6 &= 6,\\
4 + x_1x_3 &= 21, \text{so } x_1x_3 = 17,\\
-xa &= 2x_1x_3 = 34, \text{so } a = -34.
\end{align*}
